+## D15. Fresh-agent extension: GOOGL, NVDA, DIS, BP, SONY (decided 2026-11-07)
+
+- Decision: append exactly those five tickers, retain the original companies, and use only the user's empty
+  `sec_filings_fresh` database. Install the kit's Python 3.12 development environment locally. Temporary files and
+  pip's cache were redirected inside this repository and removed after verification. Do not commit or push.
+- Alternative: copy the setup example's database name or use the original worktree. Rejected: the user explicitly
+  supplied this linked worktree and database. Check: `pwd`, `git status --short`, Python version, the pre-migration
+  information-schema query (no public tables), and `extension-2026-11-07-audit.log` (`current_database()`).
+- Decision: preserve the company/CIK separation. Add Google Inc. (1288776), valid_to 2015-10-02, to GOOGL;
+  add TWDC Enterprises 18 Corp. (1001039), valid_to 2019-03-20, and Disney Enterprises Inc. (29082), valid_to
+  1996-02-09, to DIS. These dates mark succession, not exclusion of filings accepted later. Investigate predecessor
+  chains recursively, including old 8-B registrations, not just the latest 8-K12B.
+- Alternative: trust a green ticker-only first backfill (GOOGL had only 11 annual originals, DIS only 7), or
+  include every acquisition target. Rejected: the successor-issuer documents identify the Disney/Google lineage;
+  acquired businesses are not automatically the ticker's own reporting history. Checks: the SEC company-name lookup,
+  each submissions JSON and every history page it lists, Alphabet's 2015-10-02 8-K12B, Disney's 2019-03-20 8-K12B
+  explanatory note, the 1995 8-B12B and the joint 1996-02-09 8-K. URLs are in `overrides.toml`; extracts are in
+  `docs/evidence/extension-2026-11-07-*-metadata.log`, `*-covers-and-reorganisations.log`, and
+  `*-merger-and-fallback-covers.log`. The 2019 report's earliest-event date (March 15) is not the merger date.
+- Decision: rerun backfill after adding predecessors. Alternative: follow step 4 with daily run alone. Rejected:
+  `loader.ingest_filer` reads older pages only when backfill is true. Contrary to AGENTS step 2, the implementation
+  rereads all configured CIKs' older pages on every backfill (flow.py:69-71, loader.py:242-247). Live evidence:
+  initial backfill fetched 128 requests; predecessor backfill fetched 135 requests and inserted 172 additional rows.
+- Decision: no new fiscal-year-end overrides. Keep SEC metadata: GOOGL 1231, NVDA 0131, DIS current 1003 with
+  predecessors 0928/0930, BP 1231, SONY 0331. BP and SONY have 20-Fs and 6-Ks but no 10-K/10-Q in all listed
+  submissions pages; retain D1's exclusion of 6-K. Their old names, and NVIDIA's California name, do not themselves
+  establish a different CIK. Alternative: assume missing quarters or 52/53-week date drift need overrides. Rejected
+  by the full form inventories and annual covers (`*-metadata.log`, `*-cover-summary.log`).
+- Decision: retain the fiscal rule, adding real Disney October/September year-end and January-Q1 regression cases,
+  NVIDIA 52/53-week examples and its five filing-date fallbacks to `tests/test_fiscal.py`. The five fallback covers
+  confirm periods July 29 / October 28 2007 and January 27 / July 27 / October 26 2008. Alternative: change the
+  global rule or the nominal year end for one old filing. Rejected: the covers support the existing labels.
+- Decision: accept exactly five new `labels_match_sec` anomalies, by accession: Disney's three 2022 10-Qs
+  (0001744489-22-000059, 0001744489-22-000100, 0001744489-22-000161) tagged FY in companyfacts, and NVIDIA's 0001045810-10-000018 and
+  0001045810-10-000029 tagged 2010 Q2/Q3 instead of 2011 Q1/Q2. Alternative: accept all differences or alter labels
+  to match companyfacts. Rejected: actual covers and NVIDIA's fiscal-year notes support our quarters. Each complete
+  accession and cover URL is in `overrides.toml`; the check is `*-sec-disagreement-covers.log` and
+  `*-sec-cover-summary.log`. Original four accepted findings are unchanged.
+- Caveat: the check automatically calls any same-period one-year difference a naming convention. NVIDIA's checked
+  2011 annual cover explicitly calls the year ended January 30, 2011 "FISCAL YEAR 2011", while companyfacts says
+  2010. Thus the printed naming-convention count is a heuristic, not proof of the issuer's convention. No labels
+  were overwritten. Sony's latest cover was checked directly even though companyfacts does not label that accession.
+  Comparison coverage by company is in `extension-2026-11-07-audit.log`.
+- Check for ingestion completeness: `python docs/evidence/tools/extension_audit.py reconcile` independently compares
+  literal tracked-form accession sets from all stored submissions pages with `filings` plus co-registrants. All
+  eight new-company CIKs have empty missing/unexpected sets (`*-reconciliation.log`). Annual spot-check commands and
+  their actual output are in `*-annual-spot-checks.log`. This proves source ingestion, not label correctness.
+
+## D16. Do not accept a wrong Disney fiscal year to make the kit pass (blocked 2026-11-07)
+
+- Decision: stop the documented extension path with the hard check failing, rather than pretend "done". Keep all
+  source data, predecessor overrides, tested additions and evidence for the next agent. Do not add a
+  `labels_unique` acceptance, remove the Disney predecessor, update the database by hand, or invent an unsupported
+  TOML override. No production code or schema was changed in this handover-kit exercise.
+- Why: accession 0001193125-09-100081, filed 2009-05-05, has submissions reportDate 2008-03-28. Its actual cover
+  says March 28, 2009. The rule consequently labels it 2008 Q2, colliding with the genuine 2008 Q2 accession
+  0001193125-08-104229 (cover March 29, 2008). The `reports` view has no DIS 2009 Q2 row. A collision acceptance
+  would silence the check but not repair that missing answer.
+- Alternatives: accept the collision under AGENTS step 3, change DIS's fiscal year end, or add a new per-filing
+  correction feature. Acceptance and an FYE change cannot fix a wrong report year. A correction feature is a
+  separate implementation beyond the kit's documented inputs, not a TOML entry the next agent can safely guess.
+  The blocker is the documented extension interface, not network access or Postgres. A follow-up implementation
+  must preserve raw SEC metadata and apply evidence-backed per-accession corrections during every relabel, with
+  tests proving DIS 2008 Q2 and 2009 Q2 resolve to their own originals and replay stays idempotent.
+- Checks: `extension-2026-11-07-disney-findings-query.log`, `*-disney-findings-covers.log`, and executable
+  `extension-2026-11-07-audit.sql` / `.log`. Both originals' primary URLs were fetched directly. The available
+  override types are only extra CIKs, one FYE per ticker and accepted findings (`loader.Overrides.load:48-64`);
+  relabelling reads raw report_date (`loader.relabel_filer:343-355`).
+- Additional limitation inspected, not accepted away: four old Disney `rule_far` 10-K/A rows contain employee
+  savings-plan financial statements, not an issuer fiscal-calendar change. Their actual cover statements are in
+  `*-disney-amendment-covers.log`: 98-000028 is ABC's 1997 plan, 98-000029 Disney's salaried 1997 plan,
+  99-000015 ABC's 1998 plan despite metadata saying 1997, and 00-000012 ABC's 1999 plan. D1 keeps the raw tracked
+  forms, but the current reports view attaches them to issuer annuals by year. A follow-up needs explicit
+  plan-document handling rather than a global FYE override. The last document's generated primary URL returned
+  HTTP 404; its filing index supplied the working `0001001039-00-000012-0001.txt` document, used for the check.
+- Completion commands are still executed and preserved verbatim in `extension-2026-11-07-completion.log`, including
+  failures, plus final run/check logs. A nonzero run remains an open blocker, never a completed extension.
